 - **Cleanup:** both task scratch directories were removed. No heimdall-proto, argvdump or test-binary process, and no process with the task scratch in its command line, was left (counts 0/0/0).
+
+## X2 task T3 (2026-10-06): match highlight, help overlay, selection kept across filter edits
+
+Scope: `heimdall-proto tui` only, per the X2 task text (TASK.md). Part C replaces contract K9.
+
+- **Match highlight (A).** `internal/tui/tui.go` `matchSpan`/`highlight`: the first case-insensitive occurrence of the filter in the alias, and (at 50 columns or more) in the host, is wrapped in SGR 4 / SGR 24. The match uses the filter's own rule (`strings.ToLower`, rune for rune), so indexes are runes and `Sanitize` keeps them aligned. Nothing else in a row is underlined; an empty filter underlines nothing. Underline is an attribute, so it stays under `NO_COLOR` (the ASCII colour profile keeps attributes); `ansi.Truncate` keeps the SGR pair when a match is clipped.
+- **XTMODKEYS guard.** Bubble Tea writes `CSI > 4 ; 2 m` at start and `CSI > 4 m` at exit and cannot be told not to while it reads input. A terminal that ignores the `>` marker (pyte, the harness emulator) applies it as SGR 4, and the renderer never resets it, so the whole first frame looked underlined. `cmd/heimdall-proto/tui_output.go` `sgrSafeOutput` (the TUI's output writer) inserts `CSI m` after each such sequence. The renderer's pen is plain at those points, so this is a no-op on terminals that know XTMODKEYS. `runTUI` now takes the output terminal as a parameter.
+- **Help overlay (B).** `?` outside filter mode opens it (in filter mode `?` is filter text). It replaces the list rows with the nine help lines; the status line stays. `?` or `Esc` closes it (Esc does not clear the filter); `Ctrl-C` cancels (130); every other key is ignored. Clipped at small sizes.
+- **Selection (C).** `refilter` keeps the previously selected destination when it is still shown, else selects the first shown row. The existing scroll rule (selected row pinned to the bottom once past the first window) keeps it visible with a full window.
+- **Tests:** `TestSelectionKeptAcrossFilterEdits` (replaces `TestK9SelectionAfterFilterEdit`), `TestSelectionKeptFarDown`, `TestMatchHighlight`, `TestMatchHighlightTruncated`, `TestMatchSpan`, `TestHelpOverlay`, `TestHelpOverlayTinyAndResize` (cells parsed with ultraviolet, the cell model Bubble Tea draws from), `TestResetAfterXTMODKEYS`, `TestSGRSafeOutputWrite`, and the pty test `TestTUIUnderlineInPTY`. Red checks: with K9's reset restored three tui tests fail; without the guard the pty test fails.
+- **Harness 2.4.2:** 136/139 on darwin-arm64 and on linux-arm64. The three failures are the ones the task names as encoding K9 (`tui.filter_edit_resets_selection`, `tui.no_color` last step, `tui.large_100_filter_latency` update predicate); `tui.no_color`'s colour assertion passes. K17 measured separately with the part C predicate: 30/30 edits, p95 22.8 ms (darwin) and 23.2 ms (linux-arm64).
+- **Known gaps:** with `TERM` unset or `dumb` the colour profile is NoTTY and underline is dropped along with all styling (pre-existing behaviour for colour). The guard matches sequences within one `Write` call only; Bubble Tea writes each frame with one call. No help hint is shown in the status line (not requested; keeps the harness's status parsing unchanged).
